Intent: Stop refusing executable= so subprocess can exec a different binary than the sealed copy.
Property: ADR-0005 Decision §3 / acceptance 'executable= passed through'; run docstring: executable= is refused because it can run something other than the copy.
--- a/pep/implementation.py
+++ b/pep/implementation.py
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@
         ``shell``, ``executable`` and ``preexec_fn`` are refused: each can run
         something other than the copy. Caller ``pass_fds`` are kept.
         """
-        for refused in ("shell", "executable", "preexec_fn"):
+        for refused in ("shell", "preexec_fn"):
             if refused in kwargs:
                 raise TypeError(f"run() does not accept {refused}=")
         fds = set(kwargs.pop("pass_fds", ()))
